\section{Cost-Benefit Analysis}\label{app:cost_benefit}

Table~\ref{tab:cost_benefit} summarizes the inference cost and F1 gain of each aggregation strategy relative to greedy decoding.
Entity construction achieves the only consistently positive result at zero marginal cost (reusing the $N$ samples already drawn for quality estimation); cross-model ensemble requires $2N{\times}$ inference for a smaller gain.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\small
\caption{Cost-benefit summary of aggregation strategies (Qwen3-8B, $N{=}8$, $T{=}1.0$). Inference cost is relative to greedy ($T{=}0$, single forward pass). $\Delta$F1 reports the primary result (dataset in parentheses).}
\label{tab:cost_benefit}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lcll@{}}
\toprule
Method & Cost & $\Delta$F1 & Verdict \\
\midrule
Greedy ($T{=}0$) & $1{\times}$ & baseline & default \\
SC + MV & $N{\times}$ & ${\approx}0$\,pp & no gain \\
SC + LP selection & $N{\times}$ & $+1.39$\,pp (FN) & dataset-dep. \\
SC + construction & $N{\times}$ & $+1.02$\textendash$1.40$\,pp & \textbf{positive} \\
Cross-model SC & $2N{\times}$ & $+0.42$\,pp (FN) & positive, $2{\times}$ cost \\
SC + DALS & $N{\times}$ & $+0.71$\,pp (SciERC) & seed-sensitive \\
SC + verifier & $N{\times}{+}\text{train}$ & $+0.30$\,pp & no transfer \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

SC + LP selection is positive only on Few-NERD ($p{<}0.001$) and neutral to negative elsewhere (SciERC $+0.2$\,pp, $p{=}0.29$; CoNLL $-0.85$\,pp).
Entity construction is the only strategy that is positive on multiple datasets without additional model access, achieving zero marginal cost by reusing the $N$ samples already generated.
Cross-model ensemble breaks within-model degeneracy but doubles inference cost.

