\section{Adaptive Methods}\label{sec:adaptive}

Since instance-level selection fails (\S\ref{sec:selection_gap}), we present approaches that extract value from multi-sample generation beyond single-signal sample ranking.

\subsection{Cross-Model Self-Consistency}\label{sec:cross_model}

\paragraph{Degeneracy alone does not predict LP direction.}
The cascade identifies where failures concentrate, not a causal chain from degeneracy to selection loss.
We did not find evidence that degeneracy predicts LP gain across 23 configurations ($\rho{=}0.052$, $p{=}0.81$; post-hoc: 80\% power requires $n{\approx}85$ for $\rho{=}0.3$; Figure~\ref{fig:degeneracy_scatter}), though it co-varies with LP within fixed settings ($\rho{=}{-}0.881$; Appendix~\ref{app:per_type_lp}). Cross-dataset prediction requires LP signal quality (Appendix~\ref{app:conditional_decomp}).

